{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Exalted and lifted.</b> His name." "<b>Dweller of eternity.</b> Eternity of eternities, until a person cannot count. The meaning is eternity. The meaning of 'dwells' is that all created beings have motion, and the stars too have motion like a soul." "<b>In the high and holy place I dwell, etc.</b> The meaning is: for I dwell on high with the angels, and with the downtrodden who is on earth. (And the meaning of 'I dwell') is to revive the spirit of the lowly, or: I dwell on high to revive these lowly ones."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 57, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:59.764970327Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}